  "reason": "The current best is config_019 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, acc=0.725). The evidence strongly supports scvi_n200 as the best RNA encoder (~8% gain over pca_n2000), imagenet_vit_l as the best image encoder, transformer aggregation over avgpool (~2% gain), and weighted fusion over concat (~1-2% gain). The only untested variant within this top-performing design space is config_046 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + concat). While weighted fusion has consistently outperformed concat in prior comparisons, this is the last experiment and config_046 is the closest untested neighbor to the best configuration, offering a small chance of competitive performance while confirming the fusion-choice conclusion. All other untested configs involve a known inferior component (scgpt, resnet50, singleprofile, rna_only) and are very unlikely to beat 0.725. Expected relative cost: moderate (~3.5–4.5 GPU hours), comparable to config_019 and config_037, making it a low-risk final experiment that does not add disproportionate cost to the 66.18 GPU hours already spent."
